# rustdoc

Sources: [rustdoc book](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/rustdoc/how-to-write-documentation.html), API Guidelines C-EXAMPLE, C-FAILURE, C-LINK.

- English. `//!` only for crate and module docs. `///` on items. Line comments, not `/** */`.
- Do not copy Japanese `///` text from `docs/design.ja.md` into the implementation. Restate the behavior in English.
- First line: one punctuated sentence, third-person singular ("Returns…", not "Return…").
- Then why or when, then sections. Common headings, with plural `Examples` even for one: `# Examples`, `# Errors`, `# Panics`, `# Safety`.
- `# Errors` on every public `Result`. `# Panics` only if it can panic. Library paths should not panic (`.cursor/rules/rust.mdc`). `# Safety` is required if a later design change allows `unsafe`.
- Public user-facing types and methods need an example, or a link to one, within reason. Getters that only return a field can skip a code block.
- Doc tests compile. Use `?`, not `unwrap`. Hide setup with `# ` lines. Fence with ` ```rust `.
- Link types with intra-doc links. Do not restate the signature.
- A link resolves in `cargo doc --no-deps --document-private-items`. When a function becomes a test-only wrapper (`#[cfg(test)]`) of a `_with` form, move every link to it onto the item that always exists. A public item does not link to a private one; name the value instead (`u32::MAX`).
- A number or a bound in rustdoc names its source (Issue or PR) and the inputs it was measured on. A claim covers only what the code or the measurement shows: "no arena insert is concurrent", not "no allocation is concurrent"; "under 1% on the sets of #26", not "at most 0.7%".
- Do not document "this field is ignored when…". If that sentence seems needed, the types are wrong (`.cursor/rules/types.mdc`).
- When `Cargo.toml` exists, `missing_docs` is deny on the library crate. `pub(crate)` items do not need rustdoc.
- A new item goes before the doc comment of the item that follows it, or after that item's end. Inserted between a doc comment and its item, it takes that doc: in #319 a new test took the doc of `the_bound_keeps_its_measured_margin`.
- An edit that inserts before an item anchors at the first line of that item's doc comment, not at its attribute or signature. After the edit, read the diff for a `///` block directly above the new item's own `///` block. #342 repeated the split of #319 twice, after #328 had made the rule above.
- Tests do not require a fixed Preconditions / Steps / Expected comment. The test's name and body should show which design invariant failed.

```rust
/// Returns the sign of the orientation of `points`.
///
/// The sign is the exact sign of the predicate in the design, not a rounded `f64`.
///
/// # Errors
///
/// Returns an error when exact evaluation cannot obtain a work buffer.
```
